# Backup watchdog on micro2 — transcript (2026-10-17/18)

Goal: daily digest via LogSink on a systemd timer + failure drill proving
the alarm fires. Pre-state: hourly dg-backup.timer healthy; pilot soak DBs
fresh; 3 tombstoned pet DBs (live-fire residue, purge ~2026-10-18T22:32Z).

## Units (repo-committed templates, installed concrete)
- deploy/dg-backup-digest.service + deploy/dg-backup-digest.timer
- Installed: /etc/systemd/system/dg-backup-digest.{service,timer}, enabled,
  next fire Sun 2026-10-18 06:45:00 UTC. Daily 06:45: clear of the :17
  producer slot, reads a completed set.
- Fix during install: first revision carried ProtectSystem=strict et al;
  the service died with internal_error before rendering (manual identical
  command as dg worked). Minimal profile mirrors proven dg-backup.service
  (User/Group/NoNewPrivileges only) — full table + backup_unhealthy in
  journal after the change. Rule: match the proven unit's sandboxing for
  sibling units; strict-first is a debugging cost, not a default.

## Baseline (manual + journal, 23:20–23:21Z)
Digest truthfully reports the transient: 2 fresh (pilot, probe) + 3 stale
(tombstoned pets, last set 221711Z). Journal under
dg-backup-digest.service holds the table + backup_unhealthy + bounded
action. Exit 1 surfaces as unit FAILURE — that IS the alarm channel.

## Failure drill (aged scratch copy, live root untouched)
- Copied set 20261017T231717Z to /var/tmp/digest-drill, rewound manifest
  timestamp/created/started_at/completed_at/registry_captured_at by 2 days.
- `dg backup digest --backup-root /var/tmp/digest-drill` → 1 fresh,
  1 stale: pilot stale (its live-fire writes postdate the rewound
  coverage boundary), probe fresh (last write predates it). Mechanism per
  src/backup_health.rs:131-197: last_write >= coverage boundary → stale.
- Alarm in journal under tag dg-digest-drill: pilot named stale +
  bounded action + backup_unhealthy, exit nonzero. attempts.jsonl shows
  no gap from the drill (live timer never touched).
- Scratch removed. Live backup root and hourly timer untouched throughout.

